WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:08.892
OpenFlyScan brings reconstruction quality feedback into aerial capture. helping consumer drones collect better views before Gaussian reconstruction.

2
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.856
OpenFlyScan starts with an initial survey using a consumer drone and our mobile app.

3
00:00:15.127 --> 00:00:17.791
A remote workstation predicts regional quality.

4
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.300
Targeted reacquisition adds views of low-quality regions.

5
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.736
Initial and additional images are combined for Gaussian reconstruction.

6
00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:34.961
Images and camera priors enter Pi3X. Region-view association links each region to its image observations.

7
00:00:35.227 --> 00:00:41.707
The Quality Predictor processes geometry features and image features with separate multi-view Transformers.

8
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.312
The region descriptor guides region pooling.

9
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.656
Fusion outputs the predicted regional error.

10
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:53.132
Base supervision uses regional errors between captured images and GS renderings.

11
00:00:53.393 --> 00:00:59.537
For Sparse supervision. we recompute reduced-view features and add a missing-view penalty to Base targets.

12
00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:03.009
Regression and ranking train the Quality Predictor.

13
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.192
Here. the drone takes off for the initial survey.

14
00:01:20.917 --> 00:01:25.213
The mobile app plans and executes the initial five-direction survey.

15
00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:33.119
From the captured images. Pi3X reconstructs local point-cloud chunks. which are aligned into a common scene.

16
00:01:34.717 --> 00:01:37.617
The GS quality model predicts regional quality.

17
00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.887
The planner groups low-quality targets for additional views.

18
00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:49.599
The app executes reacquisition routes. turning quality feedback into additional observations before the scene's GS model is trained.

19
00:01:51.717 --> 00:01:55.509
Initial and additional images jointly reconstruct the scene.

20
00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:59.867
Matched views compare the scene before and after reacquisition.

21
00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:04.403
Our reconstruction shows clearer roof edges and panel structure.

22
00:02:06.967 --> 00:02:10.999
The glass roof also shows more distinct framing and surface detail.

23
00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:20.731
The reconstructed scene supports simulated flight with the AirSim plugin in Unreal Engine.

24
00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:32.511
From a close view. we pull back to reveal the reconstructed site.

25
00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:41.639
The collection spans campuses. residential neighborhoods. and urban districts. reconstructed from public datasets and our own captures.

26
00:02:41.967 --> 00:02:50.223
We will release the Gaussian reconstructions of all datasets used in this study. together with scripts for importing them into Unreal Engine.

27
00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:58.767
OpenFlyScan brings reconstruction quality feedback into aerial capture. connecting targeted reacquisition with reusable simulation scenes.
